Chapter: FixedRowTest

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites UI chapter Widget
  cites UI chapter Layout
  cites UI chapter Theme
  cites UI chapter BoxModel
  cites UI chapter FilterableList

 BROWSER-2. A row that asks for a height gets it.

 `widget-set-min` sets a MINIMUM and preserves flex, and `widget-panel`
 defaults flex to 1 where `widget-label` and `widget-button` default it to 0.
 So a panel given a minimum and nothing else stays flexible, the minimum
 never binds, and the rows split their container evenly instead. That is the
 trap the row was kept for, and the arms below are what it looks like.

 The two arms are the same list in a container twice the size, because the
 defect only shows where there is SLACK: with no room to spare a flexible row
 and a fixed one land on the same number, which is how this survives a test
 written against a tight box.

Section: Fixtures

  mk : Text, Text -> ListItem
  mk (id) (label) = ListItem { fli-id = id, fli-label = label, fli-sublabel = "", fli-icon = "", fli-tag = "", fli-tag-color = 0, fli-enabled = True }

  items : List ListItem = [mk "a" "alpha", mk "b" "beta", mk "c" "gamma"]

  listing : FilterableListState = filterable-list-new "fl" items

Section: Reading

  h-of : WidgetNode, Text -> Integer
  h-of (root) (id) =
    when widget-find root id
      is Just (w) -> (w.wn-bounds).lr-h
      is None -> 0 - 1

  report : WidgetNode, Text -> [Console] Nothing
  report (laid) (label) = act
    print-line-uni (label & " row 0 " & show (h-of laid "fl-row-0") & ", row 1 " & show (h-of laid "fl-row-1") & ", row 2 " & show (h-of laid "fl-row-2"))
  end

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    let tight = widget-layout (filterable-list-widget listing) theme-terminal (layout-rect 0 0 300 200)
    in report tight "in a 200-tall box:"

    let roomy = widget-layout (filterable-list-widget listing) theme-terminal (layout-rect 0 0 300 600)
    in report roomy "in a 600-tall box:"
  end
